# TradingAgents Ticket Lifecycle

## Modes

| Mode | Trigger | Mutation allowed |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Audit | review, inspect, no action | No |
| Planning | plan, estimate, create issue | Issue/docs draft only when requested |
| Execution | implement/fix an approved scope | Yes, scoped branch/worktree |
| PR/sync | push, PR, upstream sync | Yes, after verification |
| Release | publish/deploy/paper/live | Only with explicit approval |

## Issue Contract

- Title: `[TA-<N>] <type>: <short description>`.
- Labels: exactly one type, one area, and one priority.
- Acceptance criteria are observable and include failure behavior.
- Data issues specify `as_of`, coverage, provenance, and no-look-ahead impact.
- LLM issues specify schema/tool/provider impact.
- Portfolio issues specify deterministic policy invariants.
- Live/security impact is explicit.

Use `docs/ops/issue-label-taxonomy.md` for label names and
`docs/ops/in-progress.md` for active multi-agent/worktree coordination.

## Status

Use: `planned`, `in-progress`, `ready-for-pr`, `pr-open`, `done`, `blocked`, or
`aborted`. Do not mark `done` while required gates are blocked or unverified.

## Planning Hard Stop

Planning and audit modes do not edit product source, install dependencies,
create worktrees, push, open PRs, deploy, or modify external state unless the
user explicitly changes the mode.
